    "description": "Nestled on a flat block of Presidio Heights, 3485 Jackson Street is steeped in traditional elegance and timeless beauty. The formal entry presents classic black/white tiling & the foyer welcomes you with soaring ceilings and grand arched windows. The expansive living room exudes warmth with a marble fireplace and generous space for design and hospitality. The sun-drenched dining room, framed by garden views, is perfect for gatherings and flows into a bright breakfast nook beside the kitchen. A nod to the home's distinctive design, the kitchen features teak cabinetry and stainless steel counters. Through sliding glass doors, the kitchen and sitting area open to the s-facing garden designed by Thomas Church with a herringbone deck, cherry blossom tree, and wisteria. Upstairs, the primary is a retreat with lush views, a marble fireplace, and a peek-a-boo view of the GGB. A sunlit walkthrough closet leads to the en suite bath with marble counters and classic finishes. 3 additional bedrooms offer comfort and functionality, with the two rear bedrooms opening to a balcony. The lower level includes a gym area, office with a full bath, and a spacious laundry room with ample storage. Blocks from the Presidio and Laurel Heights corridor, this home captures the essence of Presidio Heights!"
  },
